.TH zmail "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zmail \- GUI mail client
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBzmail [\fIoptions\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zmail -- GUI mail client
Usage:	zmail [ options ]
Keys:	^P/^N select message, ^Z/^V page, Space page down
	d mark deleted, n new message, r reply
.HE
.B zmail
is the mail client of the
.SM COHERENT
GUI.
It must be run under the
.B zview
desktop.
It reads the user's mailbox
.BI /usr/spool/mail/ name
(the format used by
.BR 7mail )
and shows a list of message headers \- number, a
.B D
mark, sender, date and subject \- above a pane with the text of the
selected message.
The newest message is selected at start-up, and the mailbox is
polled for new mail every 15 seconds.
.B zmail
takes no file arguments; it accepts the standard window
.I options
of GUI applications; see
.BR zview .
.PP
The button bar offers
.B "New, Reply, Delete"
and
.B Purge
while reading, and
.B Send
and
.B Cancel
while composing.
Keyboard commands while reading:
.DS
.ta 6n 22n
	\fB^P, ^N\fR	select the previous / next message
	\fB^Z, ^B\fR	page the message text up
	\fB^V, ^F, SPACE\fR	page the message text down
	\fBd\fR	toggle the delete mark on the message
	\fBn\fR	compose a new message
	\fBr\fR	reply to the selected message
.DE
.B Delete
only marks a message; nothing is removed from the mailbox until
.BR Purge ,
which asks for confirmation and rewrites the mailbox without the
marked messages.
.PP
Composing replaces the text pane with a
.B To:
field, a
.B Subject:
field and a message body.
TAB and RETURN move from field to field into the body; ^P from the
top of the body returns to the fields.
The body understands a subset of the
.B zedit
keys:
.DS
.ta 6n 22n
	\fB^B, ^F, ^P, ^N\fR	move by character and line
	\fB^A, ^E\fR	start / end of line
	\fB^Z, ^V\fR	page up / down
	\fBBS\fR	delete left, joining lines
	\fBDEL, ^D\fR	delete right, joining lines
	\fBRETURN\fR	split the line
	\fBTAB\fR	insert a literal tab
.DE
A middle click pastes the PRIMARY selection: into a header field
(up to the first newline) or into the body at the click point.
.B Send
and
.B Cancel
are fired with the mouse;
.B Cancel
confirms before discarding the composition.
.PP
.B Reply
fills
.B To:
with the sender and
.B Subject:
with `Re:' and the old subject; the original text is not quoted.
.PP
Sending needs no mailer program:
.B zmail
validates every recipient with the password file and then appends the
message directly to each recipient's mailbox, under
.BR 7mail 's
lock file.
Recipients are local users only, at most 8 per message, separated by
spaces in the
.B To:
field; if any recipient is unknown, nothing is delivered.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 8n 34n
	/usr/spool/mail/*	mailboxes
	/tmp/maillock<uid>	mailbox lock
	/usr/hr/icons/mail.icn	desktop icon
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR zview ,
.B 7mail
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
All diagnostics appear in dialogs, among them:
`No such user: ...',
`The message is empty',
`No recipient in the To: field',
`Cannot rewrite the mailbox'.
.SH NOTES
The list holds at most 200 messages and the text pane at most 500
lines of at most 240 characters; longer messages end with
`[message truncated]'.
The mailbox is not polled while composing.
Quitting from the window menu asks for confirmation, but an
unfinished composition is still lost.
